{"n": 22, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "22.webp", "text": "BMW MAINTENANCE SYSTEM\n0000249 BMW Engine Oil Service\n\nReplace engine oll and oil fitter at operating temperature.\n\n324 d, td:\nDrain water trap.\n\n325 IX:\nCheck / correct adjustment of throttle valve drive (not\napplicable atter Introduction of M 1.1).\n\nlenportant!\n\nService Indicator (SI) must be reset atier an Oll Service:\nSwitch oft all electrical equipment.\n\nTurn on ignition — do not run engine.\n\nUse SI-R* with adapter** for large (20-pin) diagnosis socket\nand plug in diagnosis socket.\n\nPush In and hold yellow OIL SERVICE*** button - green lamp\n\n(function control) comes on.\n\nYellow lamp also comes on after approx. 10 seconds and goes\n\nout after approx. 3 seconds.\nRelease Oil SERVICE button — green lamp goes out.\n\nChecking Service Indicator (SI) After 10 Seconds:\n\nAt least one (but more than previously) green diode light must\ncome on. Yellow (possibly red) diode light and Ol SERVICE\n\nsign must go out.\n\nGradual Introduction of a new SI display with clock symbol and\n\nonly one red diode light since January, 1986. All five green\ndiode lights come on after resetting the Oll Service.\n\n* SER = Service Indicator Resetter, Order No. 62 1 100.\n\n“+ Adapter, Order No. 62 1 140.\n\n“** Caution!\nResetting with the wrong button cannot be corrected.\n\nService intervals would be mixed up — also refer to BMW\n\nTechnik information of Group 62.\n\n324 d:\n2 x Oll Service between Inspection Intervals for diesels.\n\n00-15\n\nGeneral Information\n\nTechnical Nominal Operating\nData Values Fluids Important Information!", "words": [["BMW", 0.0993, 0.122, 0.1236, 0.1326], ["MAINTENANCE", 0.1277, 0.1227, 0.2042, 0.1333], ["SYSTEM", 0.2087, 0.1227, 0.2518, 0.134], ["0000249", 0.0983, 0.1532, 0.1449, 0.1645], ["BMW", 0.157, 0.1532, 0.1829, 0.1645], ["Engine", 0.1864, 0.1538, 0.2219, 0.1671], ["Oil", 0.2254, 0.1538, 0.2396, 0.1651], ["Service", 0.2432, 0.1538, 0.2806, 0.1651], ["Replace", 0